From: "Christopher M. Smith"
 <25436950+theChristopher16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:43:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Stop reset when acquiring a power reference
 fails

pvr_power_reset() only warns when pvr_power_get_clear() fails, then
continues into reset callbacks and eventually calls pvr_power_put()
without owning the corresponding runtime-PM reference.

Return the acquisition/recovery error before taking reset_sem. Leave
the existing helper's recovery attempt and successful reset path intact,
and document that this prerequisite failure does not mark the GPU lost.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c
index 57f4994c28f5..54dba0ae18c6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_power.c
@@ -506,7 +506,9 @@ pvr_power_get_clear(struct pvr_device *pvr_dev)
  * If @hard_reset is %false and the FW processor fails to respond during the reset process, this
  * function will attempt a hard reset.
  *
- * If a hard reset fails then the GPU device is reported as lost.
+ * If a power reference cannot be acquired, return without starting the reset
+ * or changing the device lost state. Otherwise, if a hard reset fails then
+ * the GPU device is reported as lost.
  *
  * Returns:
  *  * 0 on success, or
@@ -522,7 +524,9 @@ pvr_power_reset(struct pvr_device *pvr_dev, bool hard_reset)
 	 * Take a power reference during the reset. This should prevent any interference with the
 	 * power state during reset.
 	 */
-	WARN_ON(pvr_power_get_clear(pvr_dev));
+	err = pvr_power_get_clear(pvr_dev);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
 
 	down_write(&pvr_dev->reset_sem);
 
